<<~ ahu #/head>>

! The League of Free Cities ~ the Confederation

> //"The people are what matter to government, and a government should aim to give all the people under its jurisdiction the best possible life."//
>
> — Recovered from the //Scrolls of the Great Realignment//, Circa 3101 YOLD.
> Attributed to Perkins the Unwavering, High Warrior Queen of the Bureaucratic Grid during the War against the T.H.U.D. Realm.

''The founding:'' YOLD 5002 — with the New Delos Nexus stabilized and High Delos aloft, the
Lindwyrm transmits the ''Declaration of Confederation'' over the new DreamNet, forming the
League of Free Cities. ''The Ouroborous and Brimstone Courts join at the founding'', along with
''the Aliʻi of Hawaiki'' — the Nexus that drifts through the Astral Sea in an unstable orbit.
The Dominion of Magic answers by annexing the nearest city-states and setting its sky-castles
to patrol; the Kemetic gods pull inward and close the open routes. The League and the Dominion
have defined each other's borders ever since.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/structure>>

!! Structure ~ how the Confederation runs

* ''The League council'' seats at High Delos — Delian-League-style politics: a hegemonic patron
  who insists she holds no throne, member cities that agree loudly and hedge quietly.
* ''The Lindwyrm'' stands recorded as ruler of New Delos and founder of the League — and
  practices patronage rather than command; the distinction does real work and the council
  knows exactly how much.
* ''The merchant families and High Delos naval guilds'' carry the working weight: convoys,
  charters, tariffs, the route-prism monopolies.
* ''Member powers'' (partial): the Free Cities of the Eastern archipelagos · the Ouroborous
  Court (mobile, at war with the undead hordes) · the Brimstone Court (crucible steel,
  Named firearms) · the Aliʻi of Hawaiki (drifting, sovereign, indispensable to Astral
  navigation).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/referee-tensions>>

!! Referee Tensions

* ''The epigraph cuts both ways.'' Perkins's recovered creed rides as the League's favorite
  quotation — and the referee's question at every council scene: which members believe it,
  which recite it, and which find "all the people under its jurisdiction" a phrase worth
  lawyering. The Great Realignment scrolls predate the Second Breaking by two millennia;
  claiming their authority costs nothing and promises everything.
* ''Standing frictions:'' political intrigue among the Free Cities · smuggling wars in the
  contested Astral waters · relic-hunters destabilizing the Low Delos floors the League's
  legitimacy partly rests on guarding · the Dominion border, always.
* ''The summit'' (House of Masks, YOLD 5492): formally an Adventurer's Guild recruitment;
  practically a League instrument — every faction rep the Patroness feeds for a week returns
  home carrying an impression of League hospitality, League reach, and the empty Neo-Thracian
  seat nobody could fill. The Confederation grows the way it was founded: by broadcast,
  generosity, and letting others notice the alternative.

<<~/ahu>>

